d excludes its\nreconstruction claims. Schema-valid corruptions must fail semantic validation.\n\n| Decision | Primary criterion | Veto diagnostics | Main uncertainty | Next action | Not concluded |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {decision} for bounded engineering conformance | independent frontends, changed inputs and rejection coverage | missing obligations={len(missing)}, failures={len(result.failures)+len(result.errors)}, protected changes={len(protection)+len(worker_changes)} | unimplemented language breadth and domain acceptance | independent result review | whole G2/G12/G15 closure, accounting or forecasting validity |\n\nSpecification is the versioned profile. Implemented behavior is in the two versioned\nmodules. Tested invariants are the executed catalog obligations. Accounting validity,\nempirical forecasting and human acceptance remain separate and unestablished.\nAll MC01–MC35 and G1–G18 retain wider obligations.\n\nThe strongest alternative explanation for frontend agreement is a shared compiler\nbug; independent arithmetic, authored-field comparison and schema-valid corruptions\nreduce that risk without proving the general language. The weakest evidence is\ncoverage outside this debt profile. A counterexample within the declared profile\nwould overturn this engineering acceptance and trigger a focused repair.\n\nActual checker command: `{payload['manifest']['command']}`.\nEnvironment: Python {platform.python_version()}, Lark {version('lark')}, jsonschema\n{version('jsonschema')}; deterministic CPU execution, no random seed or GPU use.\nWall time: {payload['manifest']['wall_seconds']} seconds. Git commit unavailable;\nsource and protected-input hashes are in conformance.json. No package installation.\nThe standalone required unittest command was also run; its final outcome is recorded\nin progress.md. Changed code, tests and profile/catalog files are enumerated in the\nmanifest. Historical controller/P02 changes predate this worker.\n\nResiduals: general packages, events, rules, postings, arbitrary mappings, multiple\nentities/books/observations, currencies/calendars, cross-company concepts, extraction\nuncertainty, accounting elections, estimates, behavior, future innovations and\nprobability measures remain unsupported. Families remain Unknown/PartialSearch with\nzero completed cells, one unsearched cell and no invented witnesses or solver results.\n''')\n    print(json.dumps({'passed':passed,'methods':result.testsRun,'obligations':len(observed),'missing':missing,\n          'failures':len(result.failures)+len(result.errors),'protected_changes':protection+worker_changes}))\n    return 0 if passed else 1\n\nif __name__=='__main__':sys.exit(main())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
