{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '9,47p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md; sed -n '30,70p' scripts/check_accounting_p03.py; rg -n 'MC02|MC04|MC10|MC20|MC23|MC24' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Repair execution audit\n\nThe approved P03 plan remains the implementation boundary. Inspection of the\ntimed-out attempt found two partial modules and no tests or deliverables. Its\nsuccessful example compile was insufficient: global constraints were dropped,\nrates were treated as dimensionless, and acceptance, package and domain checks\nwere incomplete. These are implementation failures, not evidence against the\nlanguage design. Repair them before accepting the slice.\n\nThe baseline is `borrowing.acc`, plus documented corresponding fields of the\nauthored IR, whose reconstruction claims are excluded. Independently constructed\ntyped programs and exact arithmetic checks supplement agreement between frontends.\nSchema validity is a prerequisite, not semantic acceptance. Negative IR cases must\nbe structurally valid before testing the intended semantic rejection. Stops are\nunexpected protected-input changes, missing dependencies, or failing mandatory\nchecks; failures trigger repair, never a passing report. No statistical, timing,\nusability, accounting-compliance or forecasting comparison is being run.\n\nProvenance of material choices: exact rationals, lexical rules and quantities come\nfrom `core-contract.md`; USD accounts and DebtMix fields come from the local\nDemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\nThe single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\nmultiple-source reconciliation is unsupported. Synthetic acceptance and admission\nrecords are supplied by the caller. Absence of reconstruction requires Unknown\nfeasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched cell, no witnesses\nand no solver results. Early diagnostics cover unit loss, silent constraint loss,\ninvented acceptance and copied package digests. A pass establishes deterministic\nengineering conformance only. Results are preserved in the two P03 deliverables.\n\nThe writable project files are the two versioned modules, checker, required test,\nthis profile, the versioned cases JSON and the two P03 deliverables. Existing\ngrammar/schema, authored fixtures, legacy validators, controllers, release-pinned\nfiles and preserved snapshots remain protected. Their current hashes are checked\nagainst phase-entry hashes where available, and before/after execution. Git is\nunavailable (existing marker is not a usable repository); no Git initialization.\nPython 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are existing dependencies. No\naccelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n    entry=json.loads((ROOT/'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/phase-entry-inventory.json').read_text())\n    before={p:hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in entry if (ROOT/p).is_file()}\n    cases.OBSERVATIONS.clear(); stream=io.StringIO()\n    suite=unittest.defaultTestLoader.loadTestsFromModule(cases)\n    result=unittest.TextTestRunner(stream=stream,verbosity=0).run(suite)\n    catalog=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json').read_text())\n    required={c['id'] for c in catalog['obligations']}\n    observed={c['id'] for c in cases.OBSERVATIONS}\n    missing=sorted(required-observed);extra=sorted(observed-required)\n    after={p:hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() if (ROOT/p).is_file() else None for p in before}\n    protection=[p for p in before if before[p]!=after[p]]\n    initial=Path('/tmp/accdsl-p03-protected-entry.json')\n    worker_changes=[]\n    if initial.exists():\n        worker_changes=[p for p,h in json.loads(initial.read_text()).items() if not (ROOT/p).is_file() or hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()!=h]\n    passed=(result.wasSuccessful() and result.testsRun>0 and not result.skipped and not missing and not extra and not protection and not worker_changes)\n    payload={\n      'schema_version':'accdsl.p03.conformance.v1','passed':passed,'profile':catalog['profile'],\n      'manifest':{'git_commit':'unavailable: existing marker is not a usable repository',\n        'command':'python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p03.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03',\n        'environment':{'python':platform.python_version(),'lark':version('lark'),'jsonschema':version('jsonschema')},\n        'hardware':'CPU only; no accelerator framework imported','random_seeds':'N/A: deterministic checks',\n        'data_version':'synthetic P03 bindings and digest-locked DemoDebt@1',\n        'utc':datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),'wall_seconds':round(time.monotonic()-started,3),\n        'plan':'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03/approved-plan.json',\n        'result':'data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/result.md',\n        'outputs':['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/conformance.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/result.md'],\n        'changed_files':CHANGED+['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/'+n for n in ('conformance.json','result.md','progress.md')]},\n      'tests':{'methods_run':result.testsRun,'obligations_run':len(observed),'missing':missing,'uncatalogued':extra,\n               'skipped':result.skipped,'failures':[{'test':str(t),'detail':d} for t,d in result.failures+result.errors]},\n      'observations':cases.OBSERVATIONS,\n      'hashes':{p:hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in CHANGED},\n      'protected_files':{'before':before,'after':after,'changed_during_check':protection,\n          'changed_during_worker':worker_changes,'historical_differences':[p for p in before if before[p]!=entry[p]]},\n      'requirement_coverage':{'MC02':'context and provenance','MC04':'separate alternatives and global constraints',\n         'MC10':'explicit historical admission and scenario assumptions','MC20':'package digest/applicability and report policies',\n         'MC23':'independent matched typed/text programs; no authoring superiority claim','MC24':'bounded parsing, binding, typing and independent IR rejection'},\n      'unsupported':catalog['unsupported'],\n      'acceptance':{'engineering':passed,'accounting_validity':'not established','forecast_validity':'not established',\n                    'human_acceptance':'pending','whole_gap_closure':False}}\n    out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n56:| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\n58:| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\n69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\n97:| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\n98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
