{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1793,1900p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py; sed -n '47,88p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md\"","aggregated_output":"def validate_ir(ir: Mapping[str, Any], bindings: CompileBindings,\n                *, schema: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None) -> ValidationResult:\n    \"\"\"Validate closed-schema shape and independent Core0.1 semantics.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(ir, Mapping):\n        return ValidationResult(False, (_invalid(\"StructuralError\", \"IR must be a mapping\", \"ir\"),))\n    try:\n        _validate_bindings(bindings)\n    except _Failure as exc:\n        return ValidationResult(False, (exc.diagnostic,))\n    schema = schema or _load_schema()\n    if jsonschema is None:\n        return ValidationResult(False, (_invalid(\"MissingDependency\", \"jsonschema is required for closed-schema validation\", \"validator\"),))\n    try:\n        jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema).validate(ir)\n    except jsonschema.ValidationError as exc:\n        return ValidationResult(False, (_invalid(\"StructuralError\", exc.message, \"/\".join(map(str, exc.path))),))\n    nodes, duplicate = _nodes(ir)\n    if duplicate:\n        return ValidationResult(False, (duplicate,))\n    try:\n        packages = {p.id: p for p in bindings.packages}\n        package_rows = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"packages\"]}\n        if set(package_rows) != set(packages):\n            raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"PackageBinding\", \"IR package lock differs from supplied package bindings\", \"packages\"))\n        for pid, package in packages.items():\n            row = package_rows[pid]\n            if (row[\"version\"] != package.version or row[\"digest\"] != package.digest or\n                    row[\"basis\"] != package.basis or row[\"dependencies\"] != list(package.dependencies) or\n                    row[\"authority\"] != list(package.authority) or row[\"review_status\"] != package.review_status or\n                    row[\"implementation\"] != package.implementation):\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"PackageDigestMismatch\", \"package digest/basis differs from binding\", pid))\n            if row[\"operations\"] != [f\"{pid}/{x}\" for x in package.operations]:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"PackageBinding\", \"package operation lock differs from binding\", pid))\n            effective = row[\"effective\"]\n            if effective[\"calendar\"] != bindings.calendar_id or effective[\"start\"] != package.effective_start or effective[\"end_exclusive\"] != package.effective_end:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"PackageValidity\", \"package applicability differs from binding\", pid))\n            if date.fromisoformat(effective[\"start\"]) > date.fromisoformat(bindings.horizon_start) or date.fromisoformat(effective[\"end_exclusive\"]) < date.fromisoformat(bindings.horizon_end):\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"PackageValidity\", \"package does not cover the requested horizon\", pid))\n        entities = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"entities\"]}\n        books = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"books\"]}\n        if len(entities) != 1 or len(books) != 1:\n            raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ProfileCardinality\", \"one entity and book are required\", \"profile\"))\n        for row in ir[\"contexts\"]:\n            if (err := _ref(nodes, row[\"entity\"], {\"entities\"}, row[\"id\"])):\n                raise _Failure(err)\n            if row[\"basis\"] != next(iter(packages)) or row[\"currency\"] != row[\"unit\"] or row[\"currency\"] != entities[row[\"entity\"]][\"functional_currency\"]:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ContextMismatch\", \"context basis, unit and currency disagree\", row[\"id\"]))\n            _time(\"instant\" if row[\"time\"][\"kind\"] == \"instant\" else \"interval\", row[\"time\"][\"start\"], row[\"time\"][\"end_exclusive\"], row[\"time\"][\"calendar\"])\n            if row[\"dimensions\"] or row[\"concept\"] != \"debt_principal\" or row[\"measurement\"] != \"principal\" or row[\"time\"][\"calendar\"] != bindings.calendar_id or row[\"perimeter\"] != bindings.entity_perimeter:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ContextMismatch\", \"context calendar or perimeter differs from bindings\", row[\"id\"]))\n        for row in ir[\"sourceSpans\"]:\n            if (err := _ref(nodes, row[\"document\"], {\"documents\"}, row[\"id\"])):\n                raise _Failure(err)\n        for row in ir[\"documents\"]:\n            _instant(row[\"available\"], row[\"id\"]); _instant(row[\"ingested\"], row[\"id\"])\n        reviews = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"reviewDecisions\"]}\n        views = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"evidenceViews\"]}\n        spans = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"sourceSpans\"]}\n        documents = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"documents\"]}\n        observations = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"observations\"]}\n        for row in ir[\"reviewDecisions\"]:\n            if row[\"action\"] not in {\"Accept\", \"AcceptAlternative\", \"Propose\", \"Reject\", \"Supersede\"}:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ReviewAction\", \"unsupported review action\", row[\"id\"]))\n            if not row[\"reviewer\"] or not row[\"reason\"] or not row[\"evidence\"]:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"IncompleteReview\", \"review decisions require reviewer, reason and evidence\", row[\"id\"]))\n            for sid in row[\"evidence\"]:\n                if sid not in spans:\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"UnknownReference\", \"review evidence span is unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n            for rid in row[\"reading_ids\"]:\n                if not rid.startswith(\"reading:\"):\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"UnknownReference\", \"review reading id is malformed\", row[\"id\"]))\n        for row in ir[\"evidenceViews\"]:\n            _instant(row[\"cutoff\"], row[\"id\"])\n            if row[\"system_as_of\"] is not None:\n                _instant(row[\"system_as_of\"], row[\"id\"])\n            for did in row[\"documents\"]:\n                if did not in documents:\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"UnknownReference\", \"evidence document is unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n            for sid in row[\"decisions\"]:\n                if sid not in reviews:\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"UnknownReference\", \"evidence decision is unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n            for oid in row[\"observations\"]:\n                if oid not in observations:\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"UnknownReference\", \"evidence observation is unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n        for row in ir[\"observations\"]:\n            if (err := _ref(nodes, row[\"context\"], {\"contexts\"}, row[\"id\"])):\n                raise _Failure(err)\n            for rid in row[\"source_spans\"]:\n                if (err := _ref(nodes, rid, {\"sourceSpans\"}, row[\"id\"])):\n                    raise _Failure(err)\n            reading_key = next((r.key for r in bindings.readings if f\"reading:{_clean_id(r.key)}\" == row[\"reading\"]), None)\n            if reading_key is None:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"UnknownReference\", \"observation reading is not bound\", row[\"id\"]))\n            reading = bindings.reading(reading_key)\n            context = nodes[row[\"context\"]][1]\n            if context[\"time\"][\"kind\"] != \"instant\" or context[\"time\"][\"start\"] != reading.instant or context[\"currency\"] != reading.currency:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ReadingContextMismatch\", \"observation context differs from evidence\", row[\"id\"]))\n            if row[\"domain\"][\"lower\"] != rational(reading.amount) or row[\"domain\"][\"upper\"] != rational(reading.amount):\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"SourceReadingMismatch\", \"observation domain differs from bound reading\", row[\"id\"]))\n            document_id = f\"document:{_clean_id(reading.key)}\"\n            span = next((s for s in ir[\"sourceSpans\"] if s[\"id\"] in row[\"source_spans\"]), None)\n            if span is None or span[\"literal\"] != reading.literal:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"SourceLiteralMismatch\", \"source span literal differs from binding\", row[\"id\"]))\n            doc = next((d for d in ir[\"documents\"] if d[\"id\"] == document_id), None)\n            if doc is not None and any(doc[k] != getattr(reading, k) for k in (\"available\", \"ingested\", \"uri\", \"filing_id\")):\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"SourceMetadataMismatch\", \"document metadata differs from explicit evidence\", row[\"id\"]))\n            if doc is None or doc[\"sha256\"] != hashlib.sha256(reading.literal.encode()).hexdigest():\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"SourceDigestMismatch\", \"document digest differs from binding\", row[\"id\"]))\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\nEquity roles respectively: the package report actually names these accounts.\nOther declaration names may vary. There may be multiple lets, Boolean constraints\nand conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nGlobal constraints constrain the parent family; alternative constraints stay in\ntheir respective branches and are not conjoined in the parent. No branch is\nselected or solved.\n\nBindings explicitly supply a digest-locked local package, synthetic reading and\nacceptance action, information/system cutoffs, opening balances, perimeter,\nsymbol admission, assumption periods/origins, and alternative authorship. Binding\nrecords remain separate from package definitions. Every acceptance must explicitly\nsay Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\nthe retained DemoDebt file and checks its fixed version, digest, exports and\napplicability. Paths escaping the repository and overrides are errors. The\npackage's registry examples and expected-result fields are not compiler inputs.\n\nDecimal tokens become Fraction directly; binary floats are rejected. Strings use\nJSON escapes, reject unpaired surrogates and normalize semantic strings to NFC.\nOriginal spelling and Unicode-code-point offsets remain in the separate source\nmap; typed locations identify constructors. LF, CRLF, comments and whitespace\npreserve semantics. Dates are Gregorian. All grammar words are reserved.\n\nExpressions include literals, shared references, `value(observation)`, unary minus,\n`not`, compatible addition/subtraction, numeric comparisons, typed equality and\nBoolean composition. Multiplication admits a dimensionless Real or Int factor;\ndivision requires a provably nonzero constant Real or Int denominator. Rates and\nYearFraction are dimensional; rate times money is rejected here (the general\n`simpleInterest` builtin is future work). Integer products remain integer; division\nof scalars returns Real. Addition and comparisons require equal types and compatible\ncontexts. `constant(rate)` is a scenario driver, with a constant, nonnegative annual\nrate. `external(string)` is admitted only for source/opening/report declarations.\nDebtMix principal must equal the accepted debt and opening liability, its fraction\nmust have proven bounds inside [0,1], and component rates must be constant and\nnonnegative. Interval arithmetic proves only conservative bounds; failure to prove\na bound rejects this profile and does not assert mathematical infeasibility.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
